The environment menu, runner side: report the Pod's use, and Keep running.

The composer's environment menu shows how much a sandbox's Pod is using and
when its agent exits for being idle, and only the runner knows either.
omnigent/runner/environment_report.py posts them to
/v1/sessions/{id}/environment/report every 5 seconds, as often as the open
menu refreshes, and straight away when the agent starts or stops working:
CPUs in use from cgroup v2 cpu.stat usage_usec deltas, memory as
memory.current less inactive_file (the kubelet's working set), and the idle
monitor's last activity and deadline. Pushed over HTTP rather than fetched
through the tunnel, because every tunnel request counts as activity and would
keep an idle agent from exiting. Only runners in a sandbox report: they read
IS_SANDBOX, which the sandbox image sets and the host passes on to its
runners (KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST isn't on the host's allowlist, so runners
never see it). A report that fails never ends the loop.

The server answers each report with the menu's Keep running choice ("For 2
hours", "For 8 hours", "Until I stop it"). While it holds, the runner's idle
monitor counts the session as busy and NativePaneReaper reaps no panes (its
new hold_while), so the agent's terminal and the dev servers in it keep
running, and the server keeps extending the Pod's deadline for as long as the
runner is connected. The reported exit time accounts for it. It holds only
while the server keeps confirming it: not confirmed for 90 seconds (long
enough to ride out a server restart), or answered with a 4xx (the runner was
replaced, or the session is gone), it lapses, so a runner cut off from the
server still exits when idle.
Pairs with the server patch 0015-environment-menu.patch.
Applies after 0010-subscription-in-use.patch. Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f).

